  "notes": [
    "Genuine lifecycle source form: the real header defines the virtual destructor inline and the TU defines InitResources as the key function. mwccarm owns retail D1/D0 and class data with no D2, manual metadata or forcing output.",
    "Private helper spellings (SetState, EnterState/UpdateState, the five state pairs, UpdateModels, UpdateWallAndWater, HandlePlayerCollision, DieAndDropCoins, UpdateFlight, TurnOffsetFromDist, CountSpinies, UpdateHoverBob) are truthful inferred aliases. Class ownership, inbound calls, bodies, layout, relocations and codegen are proven; the exact original English names are not. UpdateWallAndWater mangles as R10dBgCh_Actr (reference); a pointer (P10dBgCh_Actr) generates identical ARM. OnTurnIntoEgg mangles as R6Player for the same reason. SetState's signed `int` is a 32-bit register argument whose signedness the bytes cannot distinguish.",
    "daJgm_c_classInit and g_profile_JUGEM are reconstructed source-style names: SM64DS proves the daJgm_c RTTI identity, JUGEM registry ID, descriptor/factory relationship, and object shape; later EAD lineage supplies the spelling prior. Exact original SM64DS spellings are not preserved. Historical project aliases were Lakitu_Spawn and Lakitu_SpawnInfo. The factory is return new daJgm_c(); leaf operator new(unsigned long) forwards fBase_c::operator new until #2570.",
    "The retained __sinit_ov077_02127240, ctor table entry, resource BSS, and PMF state table remain separately enrolled and are not claimed by this class TU. Text-only: emitted _ZTV/_ZTI/_ZTS are licensed deadstrip-data (data objects cannot use deadstrip-duplicate); data: [].",
    "Static initializer folded: the three DaJgmModelFile handles (files 0x34c/0x429/0x42a), the two DaJgmAnimationFilePtr handles (files 0x34f/0x34d), the two DaJgmTexSequenceFilePtr handles (files 0x350/0x34e), their destructor-registration nodes, the five-pair state-table copy and the collision-offset vector make mwcc emit __sinit_d_a_jgm.cpp itself (0x25c, raw-byte-identical to retail __sinit_ov077_02127240 with the same instruction sequence, literal pool order and relocation sites); the handwritten src/unnamed/ov077/__sinit_ov077_02127240.c is retired. Definition order is the retail construction order. The vector is a JgmVector3 built by an inline constructor (plain stores, mwcc hoists mov r2, #0 ahead of the load exactly as retail) with a declared-not-defined destructor aliased at the ROM's canonical Vector3D1; the TU text otherwise never instantiates ~Vector3. The aggregate initializer copies the .data descriptors in the retail order, which the descriptors leave unlicensed. @960/@962/@963/@964/@966 clashed with ov002/ov092 and are renamed (@960->@959, @962->@941, @963->@943, @964->@945, @966->@947); atdup reports 0 cross-module duplicates. Two stale decl_common.h lines (handles, named only by this TU) are dropped per S42. This fold does NOT license the .data descriptors, the BCA/BTP pointer tables, the profile/RTTI/vtable rows or any other .data.",
    "LOCAL WORKER NOTE: this machine's stock dump is the EU image (gamecode ASMP), so the scratch link built ROM sha256 ddab9300b24aeae254192c2a30d812b07ece3adff83230e75c865ed915c9de40 -- byte-identical to this tree's stock build -- while the recorded rom.sha256 carries the fleet-canonical stock SHA-256 that every other intact entry on main shares (d1506e90...c478e8). The divergent bytes are NDS container/packaging fields outside every module range; the content proof is identical either way (moduleSetSha256 f9852ffaf80ef19662ab5535df4b13b935188ac3087b5b1d4561c089e4dd802b, symbol inventory and tuRanges all equal the canonical records)."
